Overview
--------
This project is a Java-based CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) application connected to a PostgreSQ
It demonstrates database connectivity, query execution, and schema management for Assignment 3 – Data
Project Structure
-----------------
postgres-crud-assignment3/
■
■■ src/
■ ■■ main/
■ ■■ java/
■ ■■ org/
■ ■■ example/
■ ■■ Main.java # Java code with CRUD operations
■
■■ db/
■ ■■ create_students_table.sql # SQL file to create schema and table with data
■
■■ pom.xml # Maven configuration file
■■ README.md # Project documentation
■■ .gitignore # Git ignore rules
Database Setup (PostgreSQL)
----------------------------
1. Create Database
CREATE DATABASE assignment3;
2. Create Schema and Table
CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS app;
CREATE TABLE app.students (
student_id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
first_name TEXT,
last_name TEXT,
email TEXT,
enrollment_date DATE
);
INSERT INTO app.students (first_name, last_name, email, enrollment_date) VALUES
('John', 'Doe', 'john.doe@example.com', '2023-09-01'),
('Jane', 'Smith', 'jane.smith@example.com', '2023-09-01'),
('Jim', 'Beam', 'jim.beam@example.com', '2023-09-02');
SELECT * FROM app.students;
Java Application Setup
----------------------
1. Prerequisites
- Java 17 or higher
- PostgreSQL (v14 or above)
- Maven installed
- IntelliJ IDEA (recommended)
2. Configure Database Connection
private static final String URL = "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/assignment3";
private static final String USER = "postgres";
private static final String PASSWORD = "admin";
3. Build and Run
- Open project in IntelliJ
- Build → Rebuild Project
- Run Main.java

